---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { projectContact } from '../lib/contact';
import '../styles/visitor.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="Discuss a project | Contact Fidret" description="Bring a workflow, system or project question. Contact Hadi Abou Daya to discuss the outcome, constraints and a useful bounded next step." canonical="https://fidret.com/contact/">
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="visitor-hero shell"><h1>Discuss a project</h1><p class="visitor-lead">What are you trying to make work?</p><p>Tell Hadi about the workflow or system, the outcome that matters and the constraints you are working with. An early question is enough to start.</p><a class="button" href={projectContact.destination}>{projectContact.destinationLabel}</a><p class="contact-destination">{projectContact.note}</p></header>
    <section class="contact-preparation shell" aria-labelledby="context-title"><div><h2 id="context-title">Useful starting context</h2><p>You do not need a finished specification. These details help make the first exchange useful.</p></div><ul><li>The workflow or system, and how it works today.</li><li>The decision or outcome you want to improve.</li><li>The data, access, timing or operating limits that matter.</li><li>The people who would use, review or own the result.</li></ul></section>
    <section class="visitor-split shell"><h2>Find the right first step</h2><div><p>The first discussion is about understanding the situation, what can credibly be tested and whether there is a useful, clearly scoped first piece of work.</p><p>Scope, responsibilities and success criteria should be clear before a commitment. A useful conclusion can also be to narrow the question or take a different route.</p><div class="visitor-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/approach/">How we approach a project</a><a class="text-link" href="/people/hadi/">About Hadi</a></div></div></section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
